diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 189669f..1d4d68f 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -217,10 +217,24 @@ From the repo root:
 Runtime configuration is handled via `docusaurus.config.ts`, `sidebars.ts`, and
 environment variables used by `compose.yml` (for example, `PORT`).
 
-Chat widget endpoint is configured with `REACT_APP_CHAT_LINK`.
-
-- Copy `.env.example` to `.env`
-- Set `REACT_APP_CHAT_LINK` to your chatbot websocket URL (for example, `wss://api.kumush.ai/api/v1/chat/<chatbot-id>/ws`)
+Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and set the variables below. The assistant at the bottom right of every page
+opens the personal path panel at its Ask tab; it answers from the learner's path and needs the API too.
+
+The personal path page (`/personal-path`) and its decisions and checkpoints on module pages need the
+[Personalized Roadmap API](https://github.com/mishalilia/personalized-roadmap):
+
+- Set `PERSONAL_PATH_API` to the API's address (for example, `https://api.path.example.com`). When it is empty,
+  the page says that personal paths are not set up, and module pages are unchanged. Serve the API under the same
+  domain as the site (here `path.example.com`): learners sign in with a session cookie, which browsers send
+  only within one site.
+- The path lives in a panel at the right of every page (`src/components/personal-path/PathDrawer.tsx`, mounted in
+  `src/theme/Root.tsx`): learners answer the questions, review and change their path and manage their account
+  there, next to the module they read. With a path they also see it across the course: their progress and next
+  module above the docs sidebar, each module's status in the sidebar, the decision at the top of a module page
+  and its checkpoint at the end (`src/theme/DocSidebar`, `src/theme/DocSidebarItem/Link`,
+  `src/theme/DocItem/Content`). `/personal-path` opens the course with the panel open.
+- Optionally set `PYODIDE_URL` to where coding problems load Python in the learner's browser. Empty uses the
+  jsDelivr CDN; to serve it from this site, copy Pyodide 0.26.4 into `static/pyodide/` and set `/pyodide/`.
 
 ### Troubleshooting
 
